module gunbc.plans.srv1_deploy_principal_split

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetirement, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { p }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn srv1_deploy_principal_split_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "**Goal:** remove path-unrestricted root reach from the CI job user while retaining a working deploy route. Design only, no host/workflow/sudoers actuation. Existing owners are recurring_failure_mode.the_grant_a_frontier_refuses_is_already_held_from_another_authority and rung_drop.the_job_user_holds_a_path_unrestricted_root_grant; do not file a second class. The 2026-10-19 sudo -ll specimen showed ghrunner’s whole-binary gunbc-deploy grant bypassing the narrower mask frontier. Restoration requires no path-only job-user grant and installs under the selected deploy authority."),
    p(text: "**Current authority:** D1 was decided on 2026-10-25 by the_initial_convergence_is_the_only_approval, superseding the proposed administrator-edge allocation. One broker approval per dispatch admits ApprovedConvergenceGrant; all host-root writes remain inside its claiming attempt. srv1_root_mutation_approval_is_filed_by_the_job (2026-10-26) and srv1_root_mutation_approval_run.srv1_root_mutation_after_gate own the lineage. Historical “administrator edge” instructions below mean that inherited approval, not unattended authority. One-off/off-main/irreversible work still requires the ruled scoped access-request redemption. No second deploy administrator account is justified merely by renaming the existing authority."),
    p(text: "**Effect census:** ci_deploy_access/live_deploy/privileged_effect_census own install into /etc or /usr/local, visudo/sudoers installation, apt-get and systemctl. Stage 0 added MintsHostRootReach/AdministratorEdge vocabulary and witnesses; MintsAccountWideCredential still refuses, and current rows select inherited convergence approval. Per-unit systemctl operations admit FederatedScopedGrant, but whole-binary systemctl (including edit/link) does not. Package lists need a model, not guessed argv. A grantee cannot install its own grant. Slot reconciliation is deploy authority; any job-user grant must be restricted to its own admitted unit work. runner_host_grants is already argv-pinned but installation has the same circularity. No deploy consumer was found for tailscale/rm/useradd/usermod/cp/mv in the audit read set; verify each before removal."),
    p(text: "**Tenancy is a precondition:** main-pinned fleet-converge federation materializes the administrator SSH capability only for dispatch; dev pins refuse root-host mutation and use run-scoped branch grants. That alone does not protect it from another job with the same uid: the agent survives between steps and shared /tmp/work-temp/mux paths exposed it. The read-only srv1 unit observation found no PrivateTmp/ProtectSystem/PrivateUsers/InaccessiblePaths/JoinsNamespaceOf isolation; job uid was ghrunner even though units started root. Second-slot socket access was inferred, not exercised. Removing sudo without tenancy separation would leave window-scoped root reach. D3 option b was adopted: a workflow-restricted runner group AND a distinct uid; per-job microVMs remain terminal. Any interim exposure requires its explicit drop, never a silent residual."),
    p(text: "**Deploy slot:** deploy_slot_tenancy and deploy_route_requirement own the gate. A label alone cannot reject PR workflows. deploy_slot_runner_group_subject uses gunbc-deploy restricted to gunb-ai/gunbc/.github/workflows/fleet-converge.yml@refs/heads/main, created only if absent and sealed read back through observe_runner_group_restriction. SoleTenantOfJobUid requires that restriction plus no other slot sharing ghdeploy; observer refusal or shared uid yields shared. Group-only, uid-only, wrong workflow and unrestricted group controls must all refuse. The live group/slot-unit readback frontier on srv1_observed_job_tenancy remains open; do not switch from modeled readings alone."),
    p(text: "**Resolved capacity/grants:** D4 follows the operator’s “add only if measured headroom, otherwise repurpose” ruling; host_memory_observe run 39268283480 at 0316e96614 selected srv1-02 repurposing. Re-run runner_slot_allocation.gunbc_runner_committed_width over host_width_facts rather than copying its totals: usable MemTotal minus authored overhead/session/control-plane/served/oomd and microVM memory_max/controller reservations, then whole slot fitting; never MemAvailable, swap or active-unit counts. More capacity needs a new reservation decision. D5 admits only narrow mask/set-property lines, no whole-binary grants or fleet_root_equivalent_group_names membership. D2 srv3/srv4 observation still needs the operator key before transition."),
    p(text: "**Landed model, not host completion:** runner_slot_job_role defines CiJobSlot|DeployJobSlot orthogonal to purpose; exhaustive runner_slot_job_user selects ghdeploy for srv1_deploy_slot (srv1-02). CI keeps template rendering; the deploy instance gets 20-slot-role.conf replacing CTRL_RUNNER_JOB_USER/LABELS_JSON and clearing DOCKER_HOST. runner_host_slot_role_files delivers and byte-reads it; labels include gunbc-deploy, exclude gunbc-heavy. FleetAccountDeployJob has no binary grants; deploy_slot_privileged_operations renders narrow grants as a second block in existing runner sudoers. Repurposing keeps committed width while reducing CI width. fleet_converge_host_pinned_runner_spec changes routing only when deploy_route_switch_admitted holds; unobserved group readings currently block it."),
    p(text: "**Migration:** gap-intolerant: model first; prove Y in shadow through main-pinned approved convergence with read-only/idempotent readback comparison while X remains authoritative; then one transition switches apply_dispatch, installs narrowed argv-only grants through the admitted deploy authority and deletes ci_runner_sudo_binaries whole-binary rows. No fallback or route gap. Current deploy_access_check’s principal-mismatch refusal means an alternate actor must be explicitly modeled, not assumed. Independent per-host sudo -ll readback updates the existing drop population; srv1/srv2 were known, srv3/srv4 unverified."),
    p(text: "**Consumer checklist:** fleet_posix_accounts principal/grounded intents; ci_deploy_sudoers lint/render/install; ci_deploy_access roster/commands/install scope; live_deploy.emit and extdeps.github.actions_runner comments; grounded_principal, fleet_converge_privilege_hold, fleet_converge_plan, deploy_sudoers_host_union and deploy_access_privilege witnesses; srv3_host_effect_apply/srv3_seeded_install_media and live_deploy witnesses binding ci_deploy_srv1_access. Validate live_deploy, dashboard-deploy, approval-broker-dark-install, slot reconcile and srv3 effects before narrowing. Runner group/uid witness and runner_slot_job_role_witness establish model behavior only. [Original read receipts and selection census](https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/blob/06d3c1c3149a7420c4a548b9aba9b15c721c635d/dag/gunbc/plans/srv1_deploy_principal_split.dag) retain the dated observations; host steps remain operator-gated."),
  ]
}

data srv1_deploy_principal_split_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "srv1-deploy-principal-split",
  title: "Separating srv1's deploy principal from the CI job user",
  body: srv1_deploy_principal_split_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Retires when the CI job user holds no path-unrestricted root grant on any runner host and the deploy installs run under the authority the selection names (since 2026-10-25 the inherited convergence approval), i.e. when gunbc.rung_drop the_job_user_holds_a_path_unrestricted_root_grant is retired by its restoration trigger.") }
}
